Maria Chen: Heads-up — pushed a quick patch to the API ref for POST /v1/generate. The doc incorrectly listed the response_format enum as ["json", "text"] but the runtime accepts ["text", "json", "sse"] (default "text"). PR posted: <https://github.com/redwood-inference/redwood-docs/pull/4523|#4523>. Need a docs review + update to SDK snippets.
Oliver Park: Nice catch. Can you paste the minimal corrected schema here so I can eyeball it?
Maria Chen: Sure — added it inline in the PR but copying here for quick review:
```json
{
  "request": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "input": {"type":"string"},
      "response_format": {"type":"string", "enum":["text","json","sse"], "default":"text"},
      "max_tokens": {"type":"integer"}
    },
    "required":["input"]
  },
  "response": {
    "type":"object",
    "properties": {
      "id": {"type":"string"},
      "outputs": {"type":"array"}
    }
  }
}
```
Kenji Sato: Also noticed the cURL example in the doc shows `max_tokens` as a quoted string. That should be a number (no quotes). I can fix that in the PR.
Maria Chen: Perfect — thanks. Also, the Python SDK snippet in the docs still uses snake_case for the REST example. Quick suggested Python example to include in the API ref:
```python
from redwood import Client
client = Client()
resp = client.generate(input="Summarize the following...", response_format="json", max_tokens=128)
print(resp.outputs[0].text)
```
Samir Patel: I'll update the JS example to use the JS client semantics (camelCase) and add a short note about the REST -> SDK mapping so users don't get confused. Assigning to @Samir.
docs-bot: Build: docs-site build succeeded for commit abc123 (:white_check_mark:)
Lia Gomez: Quick question — does `sse` require `stream=true` as well? We should clarify how streaming interacts with response_format. @Maria Chen
Maria Chen: Good question. `response_format: sse` is the canonical way to request server-sent events; it's equivalent to setting `stream=true` for the current endpoint, but clearer in examples. I added a note in the PR that `sse` will return an event stream and show the SSE cURL example.
Oliver Park: LGTM after Kenji's fixes. @Kenji Sato can you approve when you push the cURL fix?
Kenji Sato: :thumbsup: I'll push a tiny commit to change the quoted number to an integer and update the cURL snippet.
Samir Patel: I'll also add a short entry in the migration guide (docs/migration/v1_to_v2.md) noting the expanded enum and recommended patterns for SDKs.
Maria Chen: Thanks everyone — I'll merge once CI finishes and Kenji approves. Ping me here if you see any other param/response mismatches.
